nodecode-proofgate is a rewrite of Whydiriki700's Whydiriki700/proofgate:

  https://github.com/Whydiriki700/proofgate
  commit b07f2fe5ee019a5d6e3fd24ad3b61dbce6302fec
  MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026 Riki Wahyudi (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the plugin's three Hermes hooks and its Python modules as one
Nodecode cell. The post_tool_call hook that recorded every tool call becomes a
:TOOL point hook over the same dispatch; the transform_llm_output claim checker
becomes the proof_check tool, with the same four claim families (file, send,
run, figure), the same PASS / DOWNGRADE / BLOCK verdicts, and the same
fail-closed rule; the ledger, the /proof command, the proof_status tool and the
first-turn briefing become a JSON Lines ledger, a slash command, a tool and a
help topic. The checker is reimplemented in Common Lisp with no dependencies.

Left out, and why: the original's transform_llm_output hook held the finished
reply and rewrote or withheld it, which in Nodecode is the model's own call to
proof_check (a BLOCK in enforce mode comes back as the call's failure);
evidence.jsonl, because the evidence never leaves the process; the Python
argument redaction, because the evidence is in memory and the ledger carries
only verdicts and counts; and the `hermes proofgate ledger` CLI subcommand,
which /proof answers in the chat.
